          "ruleId": "review.witness-step-as-equivalent",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Delta, witness_small.rs step_as: `if k < 3 {Unit(id(k))} else {IMPLY_PAIRS[(k-3)%6]}` became `match k.checked_sub(3) {None => Unit(id(k)), Some(j) => IMPLY_PAIRS[j%6]}`. checked_sub(3) is None exactly when k < 3, and Some(k-3) otherwise, so both branches and the index are the same for every usize (k comes from a u8, so no overflow either way). The new test every_step_code_decodes_as_documented recomputes the expected Step from the documented rule for all 256 codes plus three literal anchors (3, 8, 9), so it does not restate the new code and can fail on a wrong boundary, modulus or pair. Read, not run."
