          "ruleId": "cuda.no-authority-found",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Query 'PTX st.global vector store alignment requirements for scatter of rows into a key-value cache' returned an unrelated cuTile SpMV sample and a cp.async.bulk.tensor excerpt; nothing on plain st.global alignment. The new gdn_kv_row_scatter_indirect kernel (dst[*pos_ptr*row+i]=src[i], one f32 per thread) is not shown to need vector alignment, and the docs neither support nor contradict that."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "The server returned unrelated samples; silence is not evidence.",
            "failure_scenario": "If the scatter is later vectorised to 16-byte stores, an unaligned cache row offset (row not a multiple of 4 floats) would fault; today's scalar stores are unaffected.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "cuda.shfl-sync-membermask",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The docs state shfl.sync is undefined if the executing thread is outside membermask (and results are undefined when sourcing from an inactive thread). The new decode_attention_split kernel scores with a warp-wide shfl.sync.down sum (its test asserts the mnemonic, decode_attention_split.rs:368). The builder helper it goes through (ptx/builder/sync.rs shfl_down_f32) hard-codes an immediate 31 in the clamp/mask position with the comment 'mask for 32 threads'; the reviewer did not verify on a device that every lane of the warp is active at each shuffle."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "source": "mcp__nvidia-cuda-docs__search_cuda_docs: warp shuffle reduction shfl.sync.bfly full mask semantics in split-K decode attention (PTX ISA shfl.sync)",
            "excerpt": "The behavior of `shfl.sync` is undefined if the executing thread is not in the `membermask`.",
            "excerpt_sha256": "d9f0fafa6f1dec1292e91b552d4cff17a832bdc0833e657eb93aec0f63dcf1f9",
            "failure_scenario": "If a tail warp of the split kernel has inactive lanes at a shfl.sync.down, the reduction reads undefined values and the attention score for that position is wrong without any fault.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
